<p>Yeah, more time shenanigans!</p>
<p>So these glasses let the wearer see into the &quot;past&quot; to an oddly specific amount of time and The Foundation is thinking they may not be looking at the past, but parallel universes that are just running slow in comparison to ours.</p>
<p>I like this one and only have one suggestion: Try giving them to&#8230;ugh, why can I never remember names, that one SCP that can see the future as she views the present. I know it mentions her in the guide to writing humanoid SCP's, but I can't remember her number.</p>
<p>I'd like to know what would happen if the SCP that can see the future at the same time as the present wore glasses that made her see the past. How much reality would explode because of this? :)</p>
<p>Edit: Found it. SCP-187 is the woman that sees the future and past as one.</p>

