			<div class="content" id="post-content-2244784">
									

<p>I'd just like to point out that crosstesting isn't something that's done on a &quot;just to see what would happen&quot; basis these days. Interactions between two anomalous things, neither of which you understand completely, can be unpredictable.</p>
<p>Basically, trying learn something about two SCP's by crosstesting them is on par with trying to learn something about two unlabeled reagents you found in the supply room of a chemistry lab by dumping them together in a beaker. Best case scenario they react in some radical way that tells you something, worst case scenario you just blew yourself up and took the east wing of the building with you.</p>

